Interactive create with ownership: none. Only an issue with neither project nor parent gets the ownership reminder, after it is created.
-- seed.json --
{"Project": [{"id": "1e000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "name": "Selected project", "slugId": "a1b2c3d4e5f6", "teams": ["0c000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001"]}],
 "Issue": [{"id": "1a000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000220", "identifier": "ENG-220", "title": "Parent without a project"}]}
-- env --
LINEAR_TEAM_KEY=ENG
LINEAR_ISSUE_CREATE_ASSIGN_SELF=never
LINEAR_ISSUE_CREATE_ASK_PROJECT=true
-- tty --
expect What's the title of your issue?
send Draft\r
expect Description
send \r
expect Which project should this issue belong to?
send \r
expect What's next?
send \r
-- run --
linear issue create
-- stdout --
{{*}}✓ Created issue ENG-221: Draft
https://linear.app/kadoraba/issue/ENG-221/draft
ENG-221 has no --project or --parent. Decide ownership from the candidate Project's full content and the related Initiative content (linear guide issue-authoring), then save the original read and set the project: (if [ -e original.json ] || [ -L original.json ]; then echo 'original.json exists' >&2; exit 1; fi; t=$(mktemp original.json.XXXXXX) || exit; s=0; linear issue view 'ENG-221' --json >| "$t" || { cat "$t" >&2; s=1; }; [ "$s" != 0 ] || ln "$t" original.json || s=1; rm -f "$t"; exit "$s") && linear issue update 'ENG-221' --project <project> --base-file original.json
-- mutations.json --
{"issueCreate": 1}
-- state.json --
{"Issue": [{"identifier": "ENG-220"}, {"identifier": "ENG-221", "title": "Draft", "project": null, "parent": null}]}
